\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{A character and its inverse}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{On a complex line, let a generator of #{C_3} multiply by
a primitive cube root #{\zeta}. Evaluation on the dual line
requires the inverse factor #{\zeta^{-1}}. The two actions
have different eigenvalues, while transposing a finite matrix
preserves its determinant. How does evaluation transpose the
[transported cochain operator](fdip-00SR), and what extra map
would identify the two fiber actions?}
